What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/<bus>-004a/touch_mode
Date:		October 2026
Description:
		Selects the stock volatile touch-controller configuration.
		Accepted values are "finger", "glove", "stylus" and
		"stylus_draw". Both pen modes use the same stock configuration.
		The default on driver probe is "finger". Reads return the last
		fully applied mode, followed by a newline. Only root can write.

		A mode change releases all active contacts and capacitive keys,
		writes the complete configuration and calibrates the controller.
		It never updates firmware or nonvolatile settings. While the
		display is blank or the system is suspended, a changed mode is
		remembered without I2C access and applied on resume. Reads return
		EIO until that new configuration has been applied.
		Unknown values return EINVAL.

		An incomplete configuration write, IRQ message read failure or
		controller reset/config fault stops touch reporting. Reads then
		return EIO; writing a valid mode while awake reapplies the entire
		configuration.
		A failed sleep/wake transition also stops reporting, but retains
		a completed configuration; writing its mode retries scanning.
		After a completed sleep, wake performs the stock soft reset and
		100ms wait, then restores the selected volatile configuration.
		Successful writes return the supplied byte count.

What:		/dev/touch_fops
Date:		October 2026
Description:
		Provides the S0226114 touch-mode ioctl interface, including
		read-only opens used by libsky_ctrl_drv.so. Command 6001 takes
		a scalar mode: 0 finger, 1 glove, 2 stylus, 3 stylus_draw.
		Command 6004 copies the selected mode to a userspace int pointer.
		Selection uses the same control path as the sysfs attribute.

		Invalid modes return EINVAL, bad pointers EFAULT and unsupported
		commands ENOTTY. Transport failures are propagated. Device removal
		makes existing files return ENODEV. Cover-mode and debugging
		commands are not implemented. The device is created with mode
		0600; stock init applies its system:radio 0660 permissions.
